\par
\b 1. Overview\b0\par
Our application "Clics" is a software-as-a-service (SaaS) platform designed to protect Google Ads advertisers from click fraud, bots, and invalid traffic in real-time.\par
\par
\b 2. Core API Functionality\b0\par
We integrate with the Google Ads API to automatically add and remove IP address exclusions at the campaign level for our authorized clients. \par
\par
\b 3. Services and Endpoints Used\b0\par
We primarily use the following services:\par
- \b CampaignService\b0: To retrieve active campaigns for the client's Google Ads account.\par
- \b CampaignCriterionService\b0: To manage campaign-level exclusions. Specifically, we use the \b mutateCampaignCriteria\b0 method to create a \b CampaignCriterion\b0 with the \b ip_block\b0 (IPAddress) field populated with the detected fraudulent IP address.\par
\par
\b 4. OAuth 2.0 Flow\b0\par
1. The advertiser logs into their Clics dashboard and clicks "Connect Google Ads".\par
2. They are redirected to the Google OAuth consent screen where they grant permission to manage their campaigns (\b https://www.googleapis.com/auth/adwords\b0).\par
3. Google returns a refresh token which is securely stored in our PostgreSQL database.\par
4. When our real-time detection script flags an IP address as fraudulent, our backend requests an access token and executes the IP exclusion mutate request on behalf of the user.\par
\par
\b 5. Data Privacy and Security\b0\par
All client OAuth tokens are encrypted at rest. We only request the minimum required permissions to exclude IP addresses. We do not modify campaign budgets or bidding strategies.\par
